PHISHING-AWARENESS TRAINING SAMPLE
=================================

Hello,

We noticed a sign-in attempt that does not match your usual activity.

For this training exercise, imagine that this message asks you to review the
activity immediately and sign in through the link below:

    [SIMULATED LINK - DO NOT OPEN]
    https://account-check.example.com/review

The message uses common phishing warning signs:
- Creates urgency by suggesting unusual account activity.
- Encourages the recipient to follow a link.
- Uses a generic greeting instead of identifying the recipient.
- Uses a sender display name that may appear authoritative.

IMPORTANT SAFETY NOTES
----------------------
This is a harmless educational sample for a phishing-detection project.
The sender and recipient use reserved example.com addresses.
The URL uses the reserved .example domain and is not a real sign-in page.
There is no credential collection, tracking, attachment, or executable content.

Suggested classifier label: PHISHING_SIMULATION
Suggested risk level: HIGH (for training/demo purposes)

Detection features to test:
- Urgency language: "immediately", "unusual sign-in activity"
- Account-security theme
- Call to action directing the user to a link
- Generic greeting
- Sender display-name / domain review

End of training sample.
